WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.100
Step 4 plans the one write.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.395
The script reads the assignments first,

3
00:00:04.395 --> 00:00:08.012
and plans nothing if the security
initiative is already there.

4
00:00:08.012 --> 00:00:11.808
Otherwise its plan holds the one
command from the guide's Step 9:

5
00:00:11.808 --> 00:00:16.114
assign the initiative at the intermediate
root in DoNotEnforce, with a

6
00:00:16.114 --> 00:00:18.815
system-assigned identity and the narrowest

7
00:00:18.815 --> 00:00:21.662
role its policies need,
instead of Contributor.

8
00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:23.218
It prints the plan's hash,

9
00:00:23.218 --> 00:00:26.950
and the security officer and
the policy owner review both.

10
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:31.889
Step 5 applies it, with the role activated
for the window and the approved hash;

11
00:00:31.889 --> 00:00:36.750
a plan whose hash changed is refused,
and fixture mode refuses to apply at all.

12
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:42.100
Step 6 is the smoke test: the policy
check shows the initiative is assigned.

13
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.600
Learn says DoNotEnforce
evaluates without enforcing.
